id: rust.grpc-service
kind: rust
title: gRPC service
aliases: grpc, grpc-server
tags: networking, serde
questions:
  - when do you pick gRPC over HTTP/JSON?
  - how do you version a gRPC API?
invariant: gRPC is just a wire format over HTTP/2; the server is a normal async Tower service that serializes Protobuf, so every Rust concurrency primitive applies unchanged.
when_to_use:
  - typed, polyglot contracts between services
  - streaming or bidirectional RPC
  - latency-sensitive internal traffic where schema-driven serialization pays off
avoid_when:
  - browser clients (no HTTP/2 gRPC in browsers; use gRPC-Web or REST)
  - public internet without a gateway
commands:
  - no stdlib command: cargo add tonic, tonic-build --features transport
minimal_example: |
  let svc = GreeterServer::new(GreeterImpl);
  let addr: SocketAddr = "0.0.0.0:50051".parse()?;
  println!("listening on {addr}");
  tonic::transport::Server::builder()
      .add_service(svc)
      .serve(addr)
      .await?;
failure_modes:
  - mixing sync and async across the service boundary (tonic requires Send + 'static handlers)
  - Protobuf schema added fields without a `reserved` tag, breaking unknown-field handling
  - streaming an unbounded message with no max decode size → OOM
follow_ups:
  - how would you version a v1 to v2 gRPC API without breaking clients?
related:
  - rust.axum
  - rust.tower
  - rust.serde
  - rust.tracing
answer_30s: |
  A gRPC server is an HTTP/2 + Protobuf codec fronted by a `tonic::transport::Server`
  wrapping a normal async Tower service: define a `[#derive(Service)]` impl,
  add it with `.add_service`, and `.serve(addr).await`.
answer_2m: |
  Code the server with `tonic`/`prost`: derive the service from your
  `build.rs`-generated trait, wrap it in `Server::builder().add_service(...).serve`,
  and treat streaming RPCs as async `Stream`s — apply bounded concurrency,
  per-call timeout, and graceful shutdown exactly as for an Axum handler,
  because gRPC is HTTP/2 underneath.
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/tonic
  - https://protobuf.dev
